  "title": "Rice Stock Declaration and Restrictions",
  "summary": "The Indian government mandates rice and paddy stock declarations to manage rising prices amid hoarding concerns, while five southern states are allowed to impose stock limits under the Essential Commodities Act, 1955. The government aims to address supply shortages and stabilize market conditions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Indian government mandates rice and paddy stock declarations under the Essential Commodities Act, 1955.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Five southern states are allowed to impose stock limits to prevent hoarding.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
